---
import Docs from "../layouts/Docs.astro";
import NotationBlock from "../components/NotationBlock.astro";
import bunkaiSample from "../content/pinan-nidan-bunkai.sfn.txt?raw";
---

<Docs
  title="Bunkai in SKN"
  eyebrow="Applications"
  description="Attach one possible reading to a move. Never treat a bunkai line as the only truth: your sensei’s teaching is the standard."
  active="bunkai"
>
  <h2>Same tree, extra meaning</h2>
  <p>
    Bunkai sheets reuse the kata spine. Number moves to match your kata sheet,
    keep Stance and Action, and replace or add a <code>Bunkai</code> line for
    the application you are studying.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Many readings exist.</strong> Label the header with whose reading
      it is (your sensei, a seminar, your notes). When unsure, leave the bunkai
      line blank and ask in the dojo.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Example: opening of Pinan Nidan</h2>
  <NotationBlock code={bunkaiSample} />

  <h2>Suggested practice</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Write the kata sheet first, without bunkai.</li>
    <li>Confirm sequence with your sensei’s version.</li>
    <li>Add bunkai lines only for the applications you were shown.</li>
    <li>Review the sheet, then put it away and train with a partner.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    Full kata example:
    <a href="/examples/pinan-nidan">Pinan Nidan (Shito-Ryu)</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
